# The data/ directory is written by 09_create_dashboard_data.R and is derived,
# not source. It is deliberately not versioned: the .rds files are binaries that
# change on every rebuild, and git would keep every version of them forever.
#
# The script that writes them is the exception. It lives in this directory and
# is source like any other, but a bare "data/" swallowed it - git never saw it,
# and a fresh clone got an app.R demanding four files with no way to build them.
#
# data/* rather than data/ is what makes the exception possible: with a trailing
# slash git will not descend into the directory at all, so a negation inside it
# never gets a chance to match.
data/*
!data/09_create_dashboard_data.R

# This does not affect deploying. rsconnect bundles the files on disk, so as
# long as 09 has been run, data/ goes up with the app whether or not git tracks
# it. It does mean a fresh clone must run 09 before the app will start, which
# is what the guard at the top of app.R says when it hasn't.
